Samejima’s Continuous Response Model (Samejima 1973), via EstCRM::EstCRMitem(): the raw response is transformed to \(Z_{ij}=\ln\!\big(X_{ij}/(1-X_{ij})\big)\), and \(Z_{ij} = \alpha_j(\theta_i -
b_j) + e_{ij}\), \(e_{ij}\sim N(0,\sigma_j^2)\), i.e. an ordinary linear factor model on the transformed scale. \(\alpha_j\) is discrimination and \(b_j\) is difficulty. The observed-scale mean response is the backtransform of this normal model’s mean through the logistic link (dispersion held fixed at \(\sigma=1\) below).


